"""Leading with AI (Leadership Edition), Session 13: Governance and buying: policy, risk register and vendors.  Practical.  Written 12 November 2026.

Based on Executive Edition Session 13 (content_exec_reference/s13.py) without the maths: the risk score is said in words and shown on a grid,
total cost of ownership is counted in shillings.  Built on Sessions 6 (vendors, data location), 9 (failures and how likely times how costly),
10 (agents, permissions) and 12 (the people plan); feeds Session 14 (data readiness and the 90-day plan).
Practical clock (bible): 10 recall, 20 idea with cases, 10 demonstration, 5 break, 60 the leader works, 10 decision, 5 close.

Cases (research/*.md): RTL-06 Kenya Airways (hook: board-approved data and AI policy), PPL-11 and PPL-12 (shadow AI, ban or policy),
LGL-07 Kenya Judiciary draft AI rules (case), GOV-01 Uganda DPPA 2019, GOV-02 PDPO v Google, GOV-03 first DPPA conviction, GOV-04 Uganda AI strategy
(draft, awaiting Cabinet, as of 30 Oct 2026), GOV-05 National Data Strategy, GOV-06 Kenya ODPC fines, GOV-08 and GOV-09 Nigeria NDPC fines,
GOV-12 AU strategy, GOV-13 EU AI Act dates as amended by the 2026 Digital Omnibus, GOV-14 ISO/IEC 42001, GOV-15 NIST AI RMF, BNK-04 Bank of Uganda
AI governance framework (case).
Demonstration: recorded runs reused, nothing re-run (demo_runs/s13/README.md): Executive Edition Case Runs F5_vendor_proposal_run1.md and run2.md
(Claude, two fresh sessions, 4 November 2026; key hidden; both caught all 11 planted flags; run 2 quoted two phrases not in the proposal).
OrbitDesk and Nile Valley Foods are fictional.  TCO figures are the Business Case Workbook example (demo_runs/s12/business_case_output.txt).
Nothing here is legal advice.
"""

